[Messages]
WelcomeLabel1=Control YouTube from any window
WelcomeLabel2=This wizard will install YouTube Background and show you how to connect the Chrome extension and record your hotkeys.%n%nYou do not need to extract files or install .NET.%n%nYou will add the extension to Chrome manually in a guided step after installation.
FinishedLabel=The application has been installed.%n%nIf you have not added the extension yet, follow the installation guide in the Start menu. Then play a YouTube video and test your hotkeys from another window.%n%nLook for the red icon with two arrows near the clock, including among hidden tray icons.

[CustomMessages]
GuideShortcut=Installation guide
OpenChromeManually=Open Google Chrome and enter chrome://extensions in the address bar.
OpenSettingsManually=Open YouTube Background from the Start menu to configure your hotkeys.
ChromeTitle=Connect to Chrome
ChromeSubtitle=Step 1 of 2: add the YouTube Background extension
ChromeSteps=1. Open chrome://extensions and enable Developer mode.%n2. Click Load unpacked.%n3. Select the folder below. You can paste its path in the folder picker.%n4. Reload any YouTube tabs that were already open.
OpenChrome=Open Chrome
CopyPath=Copy path
OpenFolder=Open folder
ChromeNote=Already have the extension? Click Reload at chrome://extensions.%n%nFor Incognito windows: open the extension's Details and enable Allow in Incognito. The guide is also in the Start menu.
KeysTitle=Choose your hotkeys
KeysSubtitle=Step 2 of 2: configure and test your hotkeys
KeysSteps1=The defaults are Ctrl + Alt + Left/Right, with 5-second skips.%n%n1. Click Open settings.%n2. Click Record beside Skip backward or Skip forward.
KeysSteps2=3. Press a key/combination or turn the keyboard dial.%n4. Set the seconds and click Save.
OpenSettings=Open settings
KeysNote=If the dial sends Volume +/−, it controls the video while hotkeys are active. Suspend hotkeys restores volume control.%n%nTo test: play a video, open another window and use a hotkey.
StopFailed=Could not close the previous application.
CloseBeforeInstall=Close YouTube Background and try installing again.
HostSetupFailed=Could not configure the Chrome connection. Run the installer again.
StartManually=The application has been installed. Open YouTube Background from the Start menu.
Uninstalled=Application removed. Also remove the extension at chrome://extensions.%nYour preferences have been kept for a future reinstall.
